WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:04.577
What this proves: the drift and
re-read clients hold read scopes only,

2
00:00:04.577 --> 00:00:08.862
and the workflow client holds one
scope and is removed after use.

3
00:00:08.862 --> 00:00:12.418
That's least privilege and
account management at Moderate,

4
00:00:12.418 --> 00:00:15.900
with the comparison kept beside
the API client's approval.

5
00:00:15.900 --> 00:00:19.337
The Graph app registration
holds only what it reads,

6
00:00:19.337 --> 00:00:23.413
with a certificate, which adds
authenticator management, IA-5.

7
00:00:23.413 --> 00:00:28.091
And no part of Pass 1 can write to
SailPoint, Entra ID or Active Directory,

8
00:00:28.091 --> 00:00:32.056
which is the Federal Modernization
Workbook's Book 13's rule

9
00:00:32.056 --> 00:00:36.410
that the coordination layer never
writes configuration itself.
